      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Race decimated by scratchings which leaves us with four runners. CALL ME COACH (2) was one of those 'believe your eyes' wins on debut at Hawkesbury in a good maiden, doing plenty wrong, getting back and wide but putting in a monstrous last 200m to win well. He looks very talented and can win. CRUDENS TYCOON (3) was a narrow winner on debut, solid again in a good BM64 last time out. He'll appreciate a bit more ground now as well. QUYNH (7) returned from a spell with fair effort last start when fourth, beaten 1.75 lengths, at Hamilton over 1200m. Will need to find more here. SHAMEFUL IMPULSE (6) broke her maiden status a week-and-a-half ago at Wodonga over 1400m, getting home by 0.8 lengths but finds a tougher race.",
